marfrit-openvino (2026.4.0~dev20260821+p8-1) bookworm trixie; urgency=medium

  * One more patch applied on top of +p7, same upstream commit (71640275),
    same smallest-sufficient-divergence numbering:
    - patches/0022: the K-quant kernel's decode variant -- packed for the
      subgroup matrix multiply on Xe-HPG (the 16 GiB card's decode launch
      3x faster), the fused path kept on Xe2 where a one-row matrix
      multiply costs like an eight-row one (measured), and the decode
      work-group sized by the projection's width on both so narrow
      projections fill the card. arcint 0.4.1 lever 1, DESIGN 7.0.2az.
    - patches/0023: the K-quant kernel's decode variant in llama.cpp's
      shape -- a work-group per group of output rows, subgroups along K,
      the super-block's quant bytes and activations as sub-group block
      reads shared by the rows, Q6_K's 2-aligned blocks as dwords with a
      shuffle, its next super-block prefetched on Xe2; exact. Faster than
      0022 on every tensor shape of the dense Q4_K_M model on the 24 GB
      card (gate projection 141 us against 170, Q6_K down projection 397
      against 646, steady state), served decode 12.1 t/s at 1k against
      0.4.0's 9.9 and 10.1 at 71.7k against 8.5, Prufstand 10/10. The
      timing test streams (eight weight buffers in rotation), warms to
      steady state and runs over the model's own shapes. DESIGN
      7.0.2bb-7.0.2bd.

