marfrit-openvino (2026.4.0~dev20260821+p7-1) bookworm trixie; urgency=medium

  * One more patch applied on top of +p6, same upstream commit (71640275),
    same smallest-sufficient-divergence numbering:
    - patches/0021: GGUF K-quant weights (Q4_K, Q5_K, Q6_K, Q8_0) served as
      stored through the fully-connected path -- a u8 constant holding the
      file's rows, an op the engine builds ("FullyConnectedKQuant",
      "arcint_opset", recognised by name), a kernel that decodes the
      super-blocks in its inner loop. No unpack at load, no reorder at
      compile, no second copy of the weights (arcint 0.4.0 stage 1,
      docs/design-gguf-native.md). Unit tests: the kernel against a host
      reference for every type, 2-D and 3-D activations; a malformed
      request refused at shape inference. The kernel is a first,
      row-per-work-item version: it opens the dense Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M
      file and serves it, at rates well under the IR's (recorded in
      arcint DESIGN.md 7.0.2ay); the subgroup-cooperative version is the
      next patch.

